INSERT INTO `policies` VALUES (1,'Booking Terms & Conditions','privacy','Jara is established only to provide the very best beach experiences - with an unparalleled experience from initial enquiry to check out. Compliance with the following terms and conditions is required to stay with us. All detail also available at: <a href=“https://www.jarabeachresort.com/terms”>https://www.jarabeachresort.com/terms</a>\n\nCHECK-IN / CHECK-OUT POLICIES\nCheck-In Time 01:00 PM | Check-Out Time 11:00 AM\n\nALL-INCLUSIVE\nThree a la carte meals are provided daily, along with snacks and popular alcoholic and soft drinks. Only food and drink provided by JARA are permitted to be consumed on site during your stay. All consumable items are subject to availability. PREMIUM COLLECTION sold separately. Customers are respectfully advised to finish all food and drink ordered before reordering - ensuring you only order as much as you are able to consume. Restrictions apply. Management reserves the right to refuse service without reason.\n\nAlcoholic beverages are served from 12:00 NOON - 12:00 MIDNIGHT, daily.\n\nCorkage is available on selected spirits and wines. Guests are required to email ahead should they wish to pay for corkage on their own alcohol. Note: no refunds are provided for [unused] corkage payments.\n\nDAILY SCHEDULE\n8:30am – 10:30am Breakfast\n1pm-3pm - Lunch\n4:30pm - Sweet Treats\n6:30pm - Sundowners\n7pm-9pm - Dinner\n9pm - Fire Pit\n​​​​​​​Midnight - Lights out\n​\nPOWER GUIDELINES\nMuseyo has no grid power. We run on a mix of generators and solar and power. All lights and plugs for small devices will run around the clock. All rooms have rechargeable fans.\n\nAir-Conditioners and Water Heaters will operate between the following times for your comfort: 5pm-7:30pm and 10pm – 10am\n\nQUIET HOURS\n12midnight to 8AM. If you become aware of a disruptive guest, please contact Reception staff immediately by room intercom or in person. Televisions, voices, and media devices must be kept at a respectful low level at all times.  Doors should be opened and closed quietly. No congregating or running in halls.\n\nCHECK-IN / CHECK-OUT\nUnless otherwise stated in the specific rate plan terms & conditions, check-in time is after 1PM and check-out time is 11AM. For early arrival before 1PM, it is recommended to pre-book early check-in. JARA may accommodate late check-out after 11AM for an additional fee; subject to room availability.\n\nREQUESTS\nAll requests entered sent at the time of booking are subject to availability and JARA bears no responsibility should it be unable to fulfil certain requests.\n\nROOM OCCUPANCY\nThe total number of occupants in a room, including children, shall not exceed three people. \n\nIf you have any questions regarding JARA\'s Maximum Occupancy Policy, our staff will be happy to explain in detail. Please also note that JARA reserves the right to refuse entry to any additional guest exceeding the maximum occupancy allowed for that room type. \n\nCHILDREN\nJARA allows a child up to two years of age to stay for free. Baby cots are complimentary upon request and subject to availability. Children aged six to 17 years old are charged at N35,000 excluding tax, daily (small bed provided, subject to availability) and food menu available.\n\nAGE REQUIREMENT\nGuests must be 18 years or older with photo identification at check-in. Guests under the age of 18 must be accompanied by an adult. JARA reserves the right to check photo identification. \n\nWiFi ACCESS\nAccess to our WiFi is free for registered guests. The hotel WiFi access code is subject to change without notice.  WiFi signals are subject to change without notice depending on location. JARA BEACH RESORT assumes no liability for guest use. \n\nDAMAGE TO HOTEL PROPERTY\nJARA reserves the right to charge guests the cost of rectifying damage or soiling, caused by accidental, deliberate, negligent or reckless act of the guest to JARA\'s property or structure.\n\nSAFE DEPOSIT BOX\nGuests are encouraged to keep their valuables in the in-room safe. JARA shall not be liable for the loss of money or other personal valuables during your stay.\n\nPARKING\nStaying guests are limited to one complimentary parking space daily. \n\nPETS\nJARA maintains a strict no-pets policy on its premises except for guide dogs.\n\nPROHIBITED ITEMS\nThe following items are not permitted in JARA\'s premises:\n-Animals of any kind, except guide dogs\n- Flammable, explosive or otherwise hazardous materials \n- Objects emitting a foul odour\n- Unregistered firearms or other weapons \n- Objects of an unusually large size or in unusually large quantities \n- Articles related to use in gambling, prostitution, smuggling or other illicit acts\n- Illegal drugs or other articles, the possession of which is prohibited by the laws of Nigeria.\n\nJARA reserves the right to refuse entry to any guest found to be in possession of prohibited items. Guests shall be solely liable and responsible for all loss financial or otherwise, and damage that may be caused by such items.\n\nPHOTOGRAPH\'S AND VIDEOGRAPHY\nUsing photographs and videos taken in the hotel for commercial or public purposes is strictly prohibited. Those who do so will be subject to prosecution. Any professional shoots would need to be prior discussed and agreed to. i.e. music videos, brand shoots, product endorsements etc.\n\nFIRE SAFETY POLICY\nThe resort is fully equipped with smoke detectors, fire safety information in the guest room welcome book including emergency evacuation plans. Please review this important information.\n\nVISITORS\nTo maintain an exclusively inclusive experience, JARA operates no walk-in guest policy for regular single/ multi-room paying. Our Day Pass is available, if booked and paid for in advance. Guest are permitted for weddings/ private (full-house) bookings, where all visitors are required to register on arrival at the Reception and are requested to leave the premises by 12midnight latest.\n\nCCTV\nCCTV systems operate in the resort\'s communal areas. Video surveillance is carried out for the guests’ and staff’s personal security and to ensure the high standard of service.\n\nLOST AND FOUND\nJARA expects guests to do a thorough check of their rooms and communal areas before leaving the property to ensure no items/ personal possessions have been left. JARA will make efforts via email to contact the guest if it becomes aware of anything that has been left, within 24 hours. It is the responsibility of the guest to retrieve any item(s) from JARA. If any item remains at JARA for more than 30 calendar days since the date of departure and no attempts have been made to retrieve the item, JARA will donate or destroy the item.\n\nHEALTH AND WELL-BEING POLICIES\n​\nEXCESSIVE NOISE AND PARTIES\nT​o ensure all guests enjoy the comfort and safety of the facilities we offer, JARA upholds a strict zero tolerance policy towards commotion, excessive noise and parties. Any person found to be on our premises creating excessive noise or otherwise causing a disturbance will be requested to leave the resort without refund.\n\nINAPPROPRIATE BEHAVIOUR\nShould any action by a guest, may it be towards our staff or otherwise, be deemed inappropriate by JARA, or if any inappropriate behaviour is brought to attention, JARA reserves the right, after the allegations have been investigated, to take action against the guest which may result in, but not limited to, being asked to leave without a refund for any services incurred.\n\nSMOKING\nSmoking is only permitted in designated areas of the resort as well as on bedroom balconies (only). There will be a N100,000 fee for thorough cleaning services charged to guest who chooses to smoke in a bedroom or indoor area, to restore it back to its original condition. The use of shisha, marijuana and other illegal drugs is strictly prohibited.\n\nIMPORTANT\nPlease be informed that JARA BEACH RESORT will not take any responsibility for and products/ services being offered or provided by external providers outside of the resort. The resort does not take any liability for accidents or other exceptional incidents in connection with the above mentioned services respectively.\n\nPAYMENT POLICIES\n​\nCURRENCY AND TAX\nRates are in Nigerian Naira (NGN) and exclude 5% Consumption Tax.\n\nPAYMENTS\nBookings are only confirmed upon fully payment, prior to your arrival.\n\nTHIRD-PARTY BOOKING SOURCES\nIn the case of cancellation or modifications to reservations made through sources other than directly with JARA BEACH RESORT or its own website, the resort recommends that guests first contact their source of booking for assistance before approaching resort staff.\n\nJARA BEACH RESORT | CANCELLATION POLICY\n**BOOKINGS ARE NON-REFUNDABLE, BUT ARE TRANSFERABLE**\n\nALL BOOKING REQUESTS (NEW AND AMENDMENTS) ARE STRICTLY HANDLED VIA THIS WEBSITE AND SUBSEQUENTLY VIA EMAIL ONLY.\n\nIf for any reason you need to postpone your reservation, the following timelines apply. With notice provided, your booking can be transferred, once at no additional cost, to a future date within three calendar months of the original scheduled arrival date:\n\n- Day Passes - 48 hours notice required (prior to 12noon two days before)  \n- One Room - 48 hours notice required (prior to 1pm two days before)  \n- Two Rooms - 72 hours notice required (prior to 1pm three days before)  \n- Three or Four Rooms - 96 hours notice required (prior to 1pm four days before) \n- Five or All Rooms - One week\'s notice required (prior to 1pm seven days before)  \n\nIf a request to postpone is received within the above required notice period:\n\n- For Day Pass visits, your booking will not be transferable to a later date, but can be transferred to another name/ group for use [only] - or booking will be lost.\n- For overnight visits, a cancellation charge will apply, which will be equal to your first night room rate.\n- Should you wish to transfer beyond three months, a fixed N25,000 fee will apply.\n- Should you wish to transfer for a second time (or more), a fixed N25,000 fee will apply for each change  request.\n\nIf a refund is provided - due to a double-booked date, or guest names not  being forthcoming for example, refunds will be  provided subject to a N5,000 admin and handling fee. Refunds will be provided within three working days.\n\nJARA BEACH RESORT is not responsible for weather conditions, personal emergencies, or schedule changes.\n\nNO SHOW CHARGES\nWe will keep your room available for the duration of your booking should you fail to check in on the scheduled arrival date. The room will be treated as paid for and occupied.\n\n---\nThis is a non-exhaustive list of general policies upheld by JARA BEACH RESORT. Should you require any clarification on terms not stated here, please contact us directly. JARA reserves the right to add to, alter or amend any of the above terms, conditions and rules as and when it deems necessary. \n\nLast Updated: 31st March 2021','2020-12-05 05:08:54','2021-07-11 13:15:33'),(2,'Photography Policy','photoshoot','We may change our Service and policies, and we may need to make changes to these Terms so that they accurately reflect our Service and policies. Unless otherwise required by law, we will notify you (for example, through our Service) before we make changes to these Terms and give you an opportunity to review them before they go into effect. Then, if you continue to use the Service, you will be bound by the updated Terms. If you do not want to agree to these or any updated Terms, you can delete your account','2020-12-05 05:09:41','2020-12-05 05:09:41');
/*!40000 ALTER TABLE `policies` ENABLE KEYS */;
UNLOCK TABLES;

